'''Genetic Apex''' (Japanese: '''最強の遺伝子''' ''Strongest Gene'') is the first main expansion of cards in [[Pokémon Trading Card Game Pocket]].

==Information==
:''See also: [[Pokémon Trading Card Game Pocket#Gameplay|Pokémon Trading Card Game Pocket → Gameplay]]''
'''Genetic Apex''' is the first main expansion released through [[Pokémon Trading Card Game Pocket]]. It focuses heavily on [[Generation I]], featuring all 151 Pokémon introduced in {{game|Red and Blue|s}} as well as the eight [[Gym Leader]]s of the [[Kanto]] region. Many of the expansions's new illustrations feature locations or characters from Kanto, and the majority of them appear as depicted in {{game|FireRed and LeafGreen|s}} specifically, including the designs of the Gym Leaders.

The expansion's three booster packs focus on three of the most popular Generation I Pokémon: {{p|Pikachu}}, the mascot of the Pokémon series and [[game mascot]] of {{game|Yellow}} and [[Pokémon: Let's Go, Pikachu!]]; {{p|Charizard}}, the final form of {{p|Charmander}} and game mascot of {{game|Red}} and {{game|FireRed}}; and {{p|Mewtwo}}, a [[Legendary Pokémon]] found in [[Cerulean Cave]] after becoming the [[Champion]] in Pokémon Red and Blue.

Several of the [[#Themed Collections|Themed Collections]] made available alongside Genetic Apex have a connection to Generation I and the Kanto region:
* '''First Choice''' features the [[first partner Pokémon]] of Kanto;
* '''Viridian Forest''' features Pokémon found in [[Viridian Forest]];
* '''Different Journeys, Different Growth''' features the first partner Pokémon and their [[Evolution]]s;
* '''Pokémon of Ancient Times''' features Generation I Pokémon that can be revived from [[fossil]]s;
* '''The Legendary Flight''' features the three [[legendary birds]] found in Kanto;
* '''Safari Zone''' features Pokémon that can be found in Kanto's [[Kanto Safari Zone|Safari Zone]];
* '''Touring the Kanto Region''' features Pokémon with unique artwork depicting them in various locations across Kanto;
* '''A Big Snorlax Nuisance''' depicts the sleeping Snorlax blocking {{rt|12|Kanto}} in Generations {{gen|I}} and {{gen|III}};
* '''The Gym Leaders of the Kanto Region''' depicts the eight Gym Leaders featured in the Generation I games and their remakes.

Additionally, the secret mission '''Complete the Kanto Pokédex!''' tasks players with collecting the first 150 Pokémon in card form, rewarding those who do with the {{TCGP|immersive card|immersive}} {{TCG ID|Genetic Apex|Mew|283}} card.

Genetic Apex was released as part of the app's open beta in New Zealand on September 26, 2024, and became available worldwide with its global release on October 30, 2024.

